“You can’t do that, Roth!”
“You called me Jamie a second ago.”
She jabbed her finger at him. “Don’t.”
It had been a slip of the tongue. He knew she called him by his
nickname when her defenses were down and she retreated into the past.
“What if I hadn’t lied?” she demanded. “What if I didn’t cover for
you?”
“Then I would have reacted accordingly.”
He watched her with such unruffled cool that she wanted to scream. Of
course, he was monitoring her. How else would he know if she was keeping
