his eyes flicked from her to the plate and then he nodded. She snorted as
she walked out of the kitchen.
The wine, food, and sex made her pleasantly drowsy. After days of little
sleep, she could barely keep her eyes open. She paused on the threshold of
the master suite and stared at Roth’s wrecked, stained bed before she
walked into the guest bedroom. She put her notebook on the nightstand,
flopped on the cold sheets, and sighed as she nuzzled the pillow.

