Chapter Six.  
SEVEN YEARS AGO.

Jasmine scribbled feverishly in the back seat with her tiny notebook
balanced on her knee and every overhead light on in the car. She
was sure the driver wasn’t happy about waiting in front of her building or
the fact that the bright interior was probably messing with his visibility, but
